# Found live: a fresh clone on a machine with the common Git-for-Windows
# default (core.autocrlf=true, global) checked scripts/vault-init.sh out
# with CRLF line endings, and the shell inside the Linux container it gets
# bind-mounted into ("sh /vault-init.sh" - see docker-compose.yml) choked
# on the \r immediately: "illegal option -". The blob in the repo was
# always clean LF; this is purely a checkout-time conversion, and it broke
# the entire stack for anyone whose global git config does this - which is
# a lot of Windows developers, not an edge case.
#
# Force LF unconditionally for anything that runs as a script inside a
# container, regardless of the cloning machine's own autocrlf setting.
# Broadened to all text files rather than just *.sh - a Dockerfile or
# docker-compose.yml misbehaving under the same corruption is the same
# bug waiting to happen, just not yet triggered.
* text=auto eol=lf
